 "The rain has been so heavy today that the pot, which I had placed beside a plant to weigh it down, had a small pool of water around its base. This has caused quite a change in the appearance of my garden, as the plants have been lifted up by the rain and are now looking rather droopy."
This journal entry highlights the impact of rain on the garden, specifically the effect on the plants and the pot. The author notes that the rain has caused the plants to be lifted up and looking "droopy", indicating that they may be experiencing some level of stress or discomfort due to the excessive moisture.
The journal entry also emphasizes the significance of the garden as a space where changes in the environment can have a significant impact on the plants and other living organisms. The author's observation of the changes caused by the rain serves as a reminder of the dynamic and ever-changing nature of the garden, and the importance of being aware of and adapting to these changes in order to maintain a healthy